        <mxCell id="case-2" value="Course study chart • Coverage evidenced by supplied slides through Class 20, casebook, assigned Realcomp reading and existing chart notes.&lt;br&gt;Read across: ISSUE → RULING → FACTS THAT EXPLAIN THE RESULT. Sources use slide numbers and full-casebook PDF page numbers (not printed book pages).&lt;br&gt;Core briefs appear first; supporting cases and litigation examples follow. Selection prioritizes cases developed in class, not every passing citation in the book. Modern examples reflect the particular course opinion or excerpt, not a complete current docket history." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf2f7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="100" width="2120" height="115" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-3" value="1. Cartels and the origins of §1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#263c59;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="240" width="2120" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-4" value="CASE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="292" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-5" value="ISSUE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="292" width="350" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-6" value="RULING / LIMIT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="292" width="530" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-7" value="FACTS THAT DROVE THE RESULT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="292" width="580" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-8" value="COURSE SOURCES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="292" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-9" value="United States v. Andreas (7th Cir. 2000)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="334" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-10" value="Did lysine producers and ADM executives agree to fix prices and allocate sales?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="334" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-11" value="Convictions affirmed; sentences remanded for leadership enhancements. Explicit cartel coordination violates §1." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="334" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-12" value="Recorded meetings, agreed price increases, sales quotas and monitoring replaced independent pricing; a sham trade association concealed coordination." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="334" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-13" value="Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 40" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="334" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-14" value="United States v. Trans-Missouri Freight Ass’n (1897)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="524" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-15" value="Could railroads jointly set reasonable freight rates to prevent ruinous competition?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="524" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-16" value="Rate-setting agreement unlawful; reasonable rates and destructive competition did not excuse the restraint. Read with Standard Oil’s later rule of reason." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="524" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-17" value="Competing railroads formed an association to establish and enforce common rates rather than independently compete." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="524" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-18" value="Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 58" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="524" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-19" value="Standard Oil Co. of New Jersey v. United States (1911)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="714" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-20" value="Which restraints and monopoly practices fall within the Sherman Act?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="714" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-21" value="§1 reaches unreasonable restraints; the exclusionary oil combination violated §§1–2 and was ordered dissolved." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="714" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-22" value="Previously competing oil businesses were consolidated under common control; acquisitions and exclusionary practices entrenched dominance." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="714" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-23" value="Antitrust Class #3_2026, slide 11 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 104" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="714" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-24" value="United States v. Trenton Potteries Co. (1927)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="904" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-25" value="Does a reasonable agreed price defend horizontal price fixing?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="904" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-26" value="No. Price-fixing convictions upheld; reasonableness of the fixed price is immaterial." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="904" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-27" value="Sanitary-pottery producers controlling roughly 82% of the business agreed on uniform prices; private control displaced market pricing." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="904" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-28" value="Antitrust Class #3_2026, slide 2 • Antitrust Class #3_2026, slide 4 • Antitrust Class #3_2026, slide 5 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 110" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="904" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-29" value="United States v. Socony-Vacuum Oil Co. (1940)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1094" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-30" value="Is concerted buying to stabilize prices unlawful without an agreed resale price?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="1094" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-31" value="Yes. Horizontal manipulation of prices is per se unlawful; market distress and claimed stabilization benefits are no defense." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1094" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-32" value="Major oil companies bought independents’ surplus gasoline through “dance partner” arrangements, supporting spot prices used in other sales contracts." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="1094" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-33" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 7 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 8 • Antitrust Class #3_2026, slide 2 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 110" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="1094" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-34" value="Palmer v. BRG of Georgia (1990)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1284" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-35" value="May competitors divide territories if they did not previously compete everywhere?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="1284" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-36" value="Horizontal geographic market allocation is per se unlawful; judgment for defendants reversed." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1284" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-37" value="HBJ stopped competing in Georgia; BRG stayed out of HBJ’s territory. Licensing and revenue sharing accompanied the division and Georgia prices rose sharply." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="1284" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-38" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 2 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 6 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 7 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 135" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="1284" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-39" value="Catalano, Inc. v. Target Sales, Inc. (1980)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1474" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-40" value="Is an agreement to eliminate trade credit a form of price fixing?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="1474" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-41" value="Yes. Eliminating a component of price competition is per se unlawful; reversal and remand." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1474" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-42" value="Competing beer wholesalers jointly required cash payment instead of short-term interest-free credit, removing an effective discount." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="1474" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-43" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 2 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 8 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 10 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 127" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="1474" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-44" value="Arizona v. Maricopa County Medical Society (1982)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e7efff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1664" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-45" value="Are horizontal maximum fees exempt from the per se rule?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="1664" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-46" value="No. Competing doctors’ maximum-fee agreement is per se unlawful." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1664" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-47" value="Doctors independently supplied medical services but collectively fixed fees for patients in specified insurance plans; claimed insurance benefits did not justify the restraint." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="1664" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-48" value="Antitrust Class #3_2026, slide 20 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 121" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="1664" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-49" value="2. Agreement: who can conspire and how to prove it" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#263c59;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1854" width="2120" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-50" value="CASE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1906" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-51" value="ISSUE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="1906" width="350" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-52" value="RULING / LIMIT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1906" width="530" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-53" value="FACTS THAT DROVE THE RESULT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="1906" width="580" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-54" value="COURSE SOURCES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="1906" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-55" value="Copperweld Corp. v. Independence Tube Corp. (1984)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1948" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-56" value="Can a parent and its wholly owned subsidiary conspire under §1?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="1948" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-57" value="No: they form a single economic enterprise for §1. This is not blanket antitrust immunity; §2 may still apply." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1948" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-58" value="Parent and wholly owned subsidiary shared economic interests and control; their coordination did not combine independent competitive decision makers. Partial ownership remains fact dependent." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="1948" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-59" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 2 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 13 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 14 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 134" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="1948" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-60" value="American Needle, Inc. v. NFL (2010)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2138" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-61" value="Does joint licensing through NFL Properties make the teams a single entity?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="2138" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-62" value="No. Separately owned teams can engage in concerted action; remanded for rule-of-reason review, without a final illegality finding." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="2138" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-63" value="Teams independently owned and competed to license their distinct logos; an exclusive Reebok license pooled decisions that could otherwise compete." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2138" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-64" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 20 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 22 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 24 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 134" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="2138" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-65" value="In re Text Messaging I / II (7th Cir. 2010 / 2015)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2328" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-66" value="When do parallel price increases support an inference of agreement?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="2328" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-67" value="I: allegations sufficed to permit discovery. II: summary judgment for carriers affirmed after discovery failed to show agreement." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="2328" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-68" value="Concentrated market, rising per-message prices despite falling costs, association meetings and internal emails remained consistent with independent conscious parallelism." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2328" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-69" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 33 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 34 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 36 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 256" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="2328" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-70" value="United States v. Foley (4th Cir. 1979)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e8f5ee;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2518" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-71" value="Can circumstantial evidence establish a price-fixing conspiracy?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="2518" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-72" value="Yes. Criminal convictions affirmed; invitation, assent and follow-through supported agreement beyond mere parallel pricing." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="2518" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-73" value="At a dinner brokers discussed raising commissions from 6% to 7%; participants indicated assent, adopted the increase, and later pressured others to hold the line." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2518" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-74" value="Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 243" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="2518" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-75" value="3. Rule of reason, quick look and vertical restraints" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#263c59;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2708" width="2120" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-76" value="CASE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2760" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-77" value="ISSUE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="2760" width="350" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-78" value="RULING / LIMIT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="2760" width="530" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-79" value="FACTS THAT DROVE THE RESULT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2760" width="580" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-80" value="COURSE SOURCES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="2760" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-81" value="NCAA v. Board of Regents (1984)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2802" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-82" value="Were NCAA restrictions on college-football broadcasts justified by the need for league cooperation?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="2802" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-83" value="TV plan violated §1 under rule-of-reason analysis. Necessary sports cooperation prevented automatic per se treatment but did not save these restraints." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="2802" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-84" value="Plan limited televised games and appearances and controlled broadcast prices; output fell, prices rose, and attendance/competitive-balance defenses did not justify the limits." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2802" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-85" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 43 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 45 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 46 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 131" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="2802" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-86" value="National Society of Professional Engineers v. United States (1978)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2992" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-87" value="Can engineers prohibit competitive bidding to protect public safety?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="2992" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-88" value="No. The rule of reason does not accept a defense that competition itself is harmful; bidding restraint unlawful." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="2992" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-89" value="Ethics rules prevented discussion of fees before the client selected an engineer, suppressing informed price comparison rather than improving competition." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="2992" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-90" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 49 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 70 • ANTITRUST CLASS #5_2026, slide 41 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 117" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="2992" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-91" value="NCAA v. Alston (2021)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="3182" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-92" value="Could the NCAA cap education-related benefits to preserve consumer demand for amateur sports?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="3182" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-93" value="Injunction against the challenged education-related limits affirmed under the rule of reason. The decision did not invalidate all athlete-compensation rules." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="3182" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-94" value="NCAA had monopsony power over athlete labor; benefits such as graduate scholarships and tutoring could be allowed without destroying the college-sports product." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="3182" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-95" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 52 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 53 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 54 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 154" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="3182" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-96" value="Broadcast Music, Inc. v. CBS (1979)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="3372" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-97" value="Is a single-price blanket music license automatically horizontal price fixing?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="3372" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-98" value="No. Blanket licensing requires rule-of-reason evaluation; reversed and remanded, without deciding ultimate legality." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="3372" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-99" value="Collective licensing created a usable package, reduced negotiation and monitoring costs, and left direct individual licensing available; it was more than a naked agreement on price." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="3372" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-100" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #7_2026, slide 10 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 110" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="3372" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-101" value="PolyGram Holding, Inc. v. FTC (D.C. Cir. 2005)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="3562" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-102" value="Could partners suppress promotion of older albums to support a new joint release?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="3562" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-103" value="FTC order upheld. The inherently suspect restraint failed quick-look review because the offered justification was not cognizable." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="3562" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-104" value="Warner and PolyGram agreed not to advertise or discount their separate earlier Three Tenors recordings; restraining those products was not needed to create the new recording." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="3562" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-105" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 55 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 56 • ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 57 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 174" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="3562" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-106" value="Realcomp II, Ltd. v. FTC (6th Cir. 2011)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="3752" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-107" value="Could an MLS exclude discount-broker listings from public website feeds?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="3752" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-108" value="Petition denied; §5 FTC Act violation upheld under a full rule-of-reason analysis. Court did not need to resolve quick-look treatment." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="3752" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-109" value="Powerful MLS withheld exclusive-agency listings from public sites; evidence showed reduced exposure and competitive harm. Equal membership fees and less restrictive alternatives undermined free-riding claims." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="3752" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-110" value="Assigned Realcomp excerpt, PDF pp. 1–2; opinion discussion • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 182" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="3752" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-111" value="Continental T.V., Inc. v. GTE Sylvania Inc. (1977)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="3942" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-112" value="Should manufacturer-imposed retail location limits receive per se treatment?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="3942" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-113" value="Vertical nonprice restraints receive rule-of-reason review; Schwinn’s contrary rule overruled. No automatic finding that the restriction was lawful." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="3942" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-114" value="A small-share TV manufacturer limited sales to approved locations to encourage dealer investment and service; reduced intrabrand rivalry could improve interbrand competition." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="3942" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-115" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #4, slide 42 • ANTITRUST CLASS #5_2026, slide 34 • ANTITRUST CLASS #6_2026, slide 5 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 78" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="3942" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-116" value="Leegin Creative Leather Products, Inc. v. PSKS, Inc. (2007)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4132" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-117" value="Are vertical minimum resale-price agreements per se unlawful?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="4132" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-118" value="Federal rule of reason applies; Dr. Miles overruled, judgment reversed and case remanded. RPM was not declared invariably lawful." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="4132" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-119" value="Brighton supplier cut off a retailer discounting by 20%; dealer services and free-riding offered possible efficiencies. Dealer-driven restraints, widespread RPM and market power can instead suggest harm." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="4132" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-120" value="Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 78" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="4132" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-121" value="4. Market definition and monopolization" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#263c59;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4322" width="2120" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-122" value="CASE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4374" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-123" value="ISSUE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="4374" width="350" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-124" value="RULING / LIMIT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="4374" width="530" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-125" value="FACTS THAT DROVE THE RESULT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="4374" width="580" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-126" value="COURSE SOURCES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="4374" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-127" value="United States v. E.I. du Pont de Nemours &amp;amp; Co. (1956)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4416" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-128" value="Was the relevant market cellophane alone or flexible packaging materials?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="4416" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-129" value="Broader flexible-packaging market accepted; no monopoly power established in that market." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="4416" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-130" value="Court relied on reasonable interchangeability and cross-elasticity among wrapping products. Study caution: substitution at an already monopolized price can produce the “cellophane fallacy.”" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="4416" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-131" value="Class #11 Market Def Unit 1_2 _2026, slide 8 • Class #11 Market Def Unit 1_2 _2026, slide 10 • Class #11 Market Def Unit 1_2 _2026, slide 11 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 233" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="4416" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-132" value="United States v. Aluminum Co. of America — Alcoa (2d Cir. 1945)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4606" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-133" value="How should aluminum monopoly power and exclusionary maintenance be assessed?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="4606" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-134" value="Alcoa unlawfully monopolized virgin aluminum ingot; deliberate capacity expansion was treated as exclusionary in context. Later law scrutinizes that conduct theory." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="4606" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-135" value="Including captive production and excluding secondary aluminum yielded over 90% share; repeatedly anticipating demand and expanding capacity left little room for entrants. Historical percentages are not universal thresholds." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="4606" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-136" value="Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 58" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="4606" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-137" value="United States v. Grinnell Corp. (1966)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4796" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-138" value="When does dominant size amount to unlawful monopolization?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="4796" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-139" value="§2 requires monopoly power plus willful acquisition or maintenance, beyond superior product, skill or historical accident; liability upheld." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="4796" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-140" value="Affiliated alarm-service companies held roughly 87% of accredited central-station protective services; acquisitions and exclusionary arrangements supported monopoly maintenance." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="4796" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-141" value="Class # 12 Section 2 Introduction 2026, slide 6 • Class #11 Market Def Unit 1_2 _2026, slide 28 • Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 4 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 167" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="4796" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-142" value="Lorain Journal Co. v. United States (1951)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="4986" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-143" value="Could a dominant newspaper deny advertising to customers using a rival radio station?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="4986" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-144" value="Attempted monopolization violated §2; injunction upheld. A seller’s freedom to choose customers is qualified when used to exclude competition." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="4986" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-145" value="Newspaper reached almost all local families and monitored advertisers; it refused ads from customers using WEOL to eliminate the emerging radio rival." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="4986" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-146" value="Class # 12 Section 2 Introduction 2026, slide 20 • Class # 12 Section 2 Introduction 2026, slide 21 • Class #11 Market Def Unit 1_2 _2026, slide 39 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 290" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="4986" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-147" value="Otter Tail Power Co. v. United States (1973)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5176" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-148" value="Could a utility refuse wholesale supply or transmission to block municipal competition?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="5176" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-149" value="Refusals violated §2; industry regulation did not displace antitrust scrutiny in this setting." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="5176" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-150" value="Otter Tail controlled transmission essential to towns seeking municipal systems and denied both wholesale electricity and carriage of rival suppliers’ power to preserve retail business." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="5176" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-151" value="Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 6 • Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 7 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 400" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="5176" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-152" value="Aspen Skiing Co. v. Aspen Highlands Skiing Corp. (1985)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5366" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-153" value="When can terminating cooperation with a rival be exclusionary?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="5366" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-154" value="§2 verdict upheld. Evidence supported sacrificing short-term profits to exclude a rival; there is no general duty to cooperate." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="5366" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-155" value="Owner of three of four mountains ended a popular, profitable all-mountain pass, rejected practical alternatives and even refused retail-price tickets; claimed efficiencies lacked evidentiary support." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="5366" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-156" value="Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 8 • Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 11 • Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 12 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 290" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="5366" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-157" value="Verizon Communications Inc. v. Trinko (2004)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5556" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-158" value="Did deficient access to a regulated telecom network create a §2 refusal-to-deal claim?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="5556" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-159" value="No claim on these allegations. Aspen is a narrow exception; regulatory duties do not automatically become antitrust duties." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="5556" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-160" value="Sharing was legally compelled rather than a prior voluntary profitable arrangement; active regulation addressed access. Forced dealing risked weak investment incentives and difficult judicial supervision." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="5556" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-161" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #6_2026, slide 13 • Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 19 • Class #13 Section 2 Otter Tail Aspen _ 2026, slide 22 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 167" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="5556" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-162" value="United States v. Microsoft Corp. (D.C. Cir. 2001)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#eeeafa;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5746" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-163" value="Did restrictions protecting Windows from browser and Java threats unlawfully maintain its monopoly?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="5746" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-164" value="Monopoly-maintenance liability largely affirmed, with some acts rejected; browser-attempt claim reversed, tying remanded for rule of reason, breakup vacated." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="5746" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-165" value="Over 95% of Intel-compatible PC operating systems plus an applications barrier supported power. OEM restrictions and browser integration impeded nascent platform threats; each act required effects and justification analysis." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="5746" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-166" value="Class #15 Microsoft_2026, slide 1 • Class #15 Microsoft_2026, slide 2 • Class #15 Microsoft_2026, slide 3 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 73" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="5746" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-167" value="5. Tying and exclusionary distribution" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#263c59;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5936" width="2120" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-168" value="CASE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="5988" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-169" value="ISSUE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="5988" width="350" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-170" value="RULING / LIMIT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="5988" width="530" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-171" value="FACTS THAT DROVE THE RESULT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="5988" width="580" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-172" value="COURSE SOURCES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="5988" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-173" value="Jefferson Parish Hospital District No. 2 v. Hyde (1984)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="6030" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-174" value="Did requiring surgery patients to use the hospital’s anesthesiology group create unlawful tying?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="6030" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-175" value="No violation established: insufficient tying-market power for per se condemnation and insufficient evidence under rule of reason." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="6030" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-176" value="Separate demand made surgery and anesthesia distinct products, but about 70% of local patients used other hospitals; a roughly 30% share did not establish power to force the tie." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="6030" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-177" value="Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 11 • Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 12 • Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 14 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 483" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="6030" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-178" value="Eastman Kodak Co. v. Image Technical Services (1992)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="6220" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-179" value="Does competition for new equipment necessarily prevent power over brand-specific parts and service?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="6220" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-180" value="No. Summary judgment for Kodak rejected; tying and monopolization claims could proceed. This was not a final liability judgment." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="6220" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-181" value="Kodak restricted parts access for independent servicers; information costs, installed-base lock-in and costly switching could permit aftermarket power despite equipment-market competition." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="6220" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-182" value="Class # 12 Section 2 Introduction 2026, slide 19 • Class #11 Market Def Unit 1_2 _2026, slide 38 • Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 8 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 156" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="6220" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-183" value="United States v. Google — Search (D.D.C. 2024)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#e3f4f5;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="6410" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-184" value="Did default-search distribution contracts unlawfully maintain search monopolies?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="6410" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-185" value="2024 liability ruling found unlawful maintenance in general search services and general search text advertising. This brief addresses the taught liability opinion, not later remedies." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="6410" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-186" value="Default placements and revenue-sharing contracts locked up major browser/mobile access points; defaults discouraged switching and deprived rivals of query scale needed to improve quality." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="6410" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-187" value="Class #15 Microsoft_2026, slide 5 • Class #18_Google 2026 , slide 3 • Class #18_Google 2026 , slide 4 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 73" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="6410" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-188" value="6. Merger review under Clayton Act §7" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#263c59;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="6600" width="2120" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-189" value="CASE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="6652" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-190" value="ISSUE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="6652" width="350" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-191" value="RULING / LIMIT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="6652" width="530" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-192" value="FACTS THAT DROVE THE RESULT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="6652" width="580" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-193" value="COURSE SOURCES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="6652" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-194" value="United States v. Philadelphia National Bank (1963)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="6694" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-195" value="When does merger concentration presumptively threaten competition?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="6694" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-196" value="Merger unlawful: undue combined share plus significant concentration increase establishes a rebuttable presumption. Benefits in other markets did not excuse local harm." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="6694" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-197" value="Second- and third-largest local commercial banks would combine amid increasing concentration; resulting firm exceeded 30% and top two would hold roughly 59% of assets." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="6694" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-198" value="Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 8 • Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 9 • Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 10 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 101" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="6694" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-199" value="United States v. General Dynamics Corp. (1974)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="6884" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-200" value="Can future competitive weakness rebut concentration statistics?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="6884" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-201" value="Yes. Judgment permitting acquisition affirmed because production shares overstated the target’s future competitive significance." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="6884" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-202" value="Coal sold through long-term contracts; target had scarce uncommitted reserves, most remaining coal already promised, and little ability to acquire or develop more. It could not compete strongly for new contracts." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="6884" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-203" value="Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 12 • Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 14 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 433" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="6884" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-204" value="Hospital Corp. of America v. FTC (7th Cir. 1986)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fbe9e7;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="7074" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-205" value="Did hospital acquisitions create a sufficient risk of future coordination?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="7074" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-206" value="FTC divestiture order upheld. §7 requires an appreciable danger of future harm rather than proof that collusion already occurred." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="7074" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-207" value="Chattanooga hospital owners fell from 11 to 7; four firms controlled about 91%. Entry regulation, limited geographic substitution, inelastic demand and a history of cooperation strengthened the prediction." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="7074" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-208" value="Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 16 • Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 18 • Class #20 _ Mergers_NA, slide 19 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 442" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="7074" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-209" value="7. Supporting historical cases and current litigation examples" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#263c59;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="7264" width="2120" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-210" value="CASE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="7316" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-211" value="ISSUE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="7316" width="350" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-212" value="RULING / LIMIT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="7316" width="530" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-213" value="FACTS THAT DROVE THE RESULT" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="7316" width="580" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-214" value="COURSE SOURCES" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="7316" width="330" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-215" value="International Salt Co. v. United States (1947)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="7358" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-216" value="Could patented salt machines be leased only with the lessor’s salt?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="7358" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-217" value="Tie condemned under the historical per se approach; patent rights did not justify extending control to salt." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="7358" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-218" value="Leases required use of defendant’s salt in its patented machines, foreclosing competing salt sellers. Read with later tying-market-power requirements." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="7358" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-219" value="Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 9 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 604" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="7358" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-220" value="IBM v. United States (1936)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="7548" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-221" value="Could IBM require lessees to use only IBM punch cards?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="7548" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-222" value="Requirement unlawful under Clayton Act §3; quality claims did not justify excluding suitable rival cards." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="7548" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-223" value="Other manufacturers could meet machine tolerances and obtain suitable paper; the record undermined the claim that exclusive sourcing was necessary for accuracy." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="7548" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-224" value="Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 9 • Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 10 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 73" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="7548" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-225" value="Northern Pacific Railway Co. v. United States (1958)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="7738" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-226" value="Could land purchasers or lessees be required to route freight over the railroad?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="7738" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-227" value="Preferential-routing ties condemned; case supplies the classic rationale for per se treatment." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="7738" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-228" value="Extensive desirable land holdings gave bargaining leverage; routing clauses diverted substantial freight commerce. The course uses it for both tying history and the per se standard." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="7738" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-229" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #7_2026, slide 16 • Class #17 _Tying_2026, slide 9 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 84" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="7738" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-230" value="United States v. Apple — complaint example (2024)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="7928" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-231" value="What does the Apple smartphone complaint allege?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="7928" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-232" value="Class 18 presents allegations, not a merits holding; no Apple liability conclusion is supplied by those slides." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="7928" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-233" value="Government alleges restrictions on apps, wallets and interoperability protect smartphone power and raise switching barriers. Alleged market shares and exclusionary effects remain allegations in this course excerpt." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="7928" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-234" value="Class #18_Google 2026 , slide 33" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="7928" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-235" value="FTC v. Meta — market-definition example in Class 11" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="8118" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-236" value="Should the market include all social networking or a narrower personal-social-networking category?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="8118" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-237" value="The supplied slides contrast competing definitions; they do not supply a merits ruling to summarize." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="8118" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-238" value="FTC proposes personal social networking; Meta proposes broader social networking. For zero-price products, quality changes can inform substitution analysis. Do not infer an outcome from the slide headings." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="8118" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-239" value="Class #11 Market Def Unit 1_2 _2026, slide 16" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="8118" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-240" value="Gibson v. Cendyn Group (9th Cir. 2025)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="8308" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-241" value="Did hotels’ use of common pricing software plausibly allege a §1 agreement?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="8308" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-242" value="Dismissal affirmed on the pleaded facts; using the same recommendation software did not itself establish a horizontal agreement." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="8308" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-243" value="Allegations did not plausibly connect independent software contracts into a common scheme; recommendations did not bind hotels. This is a pleading ruling, not immunity for algorithmic pricing." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="8308" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-244" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #5_2026, slide 24 • Gavil et al., 4th ed., PDF p. 142" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="8308" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-245" value="Cornish-Adebiyi v. Caesars Entertainment (3d Cir. July 2026)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#edf0f4;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="8498" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-246" value="Could algorithmic hotel-pricing allegations support a plausible agreement?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="8498" width="350" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-247" value="Class 5 contrasts this as a potential-agreement case at the pleading stage; it does not establish proven price fixing." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="8498" width="530" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-248" value="Alleged coordination through shared pricing software supplies the comparison with Gibson. Treat factual allegations as unproven and avoid a categorical rule that software use equals agreement." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="8498" width="580" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-249" value="ANTITRUST CLASS #5_2026, slide 24" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1830" y="8498" width="330" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="case-250" value="STUDY LIMITS / COMPARISONS&lt;br&gt;Copperweld ≠ general antitrust immunity. Sylvania, Leegin and BMI choose a standard; they do not declare every restraint lawful. Kodak is summary-judgment review. Text Messaging I and II differ in procedural stage. Aspen is narrow after Trinko. Microsoft separates monopoly maintenance, attempted monopolization, tying and remedy. PNB’s presumption is rebuttable under General Dynamics.&lt;br&gt;Historical tying and Alcoa doctrines should be read with the later cases shown above. Apple and Meta entries report only what the supplied course materials establish; RealPage is mentioned without a discrete ruling in the supplied slides, so no case holding is invented." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fillColor=#fff3dc;strokeColor=#d3dae5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#172b4d;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="8713" width="2120" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="sherman-analysis-flow" name="§1 &amp; §2 Analysis Flowchart">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1592" dy="665" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="3300" pageHeight="4200" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="start" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Sherman Act: Identify the Conduct&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Copperweld • Grinnell • Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Identify the actors, challenged restraint, affected consumers and interstate-commerce connection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Agreement?&lt;/b&gt; Analyze §1. &lt;b&gt;Monopoly maintenance or acquisition?&lt;/b&gt; Analyze §2. The same conduct can raise both.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Course framework through Class 20. Case details and references are in the Important Cases tab.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="650" x="1200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;§1 — Agreement + Unreasonable Restraint&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Standard Oil • Copperweld&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;(1) Contract, combination or conspiracy.&lt;br&gt;(2) Unreasonable restraint of trade.&lt;br&gt;(3) Interstate or foreign commerce.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Begin with who can agree, then whether an agreement exists, then choose the analytical standard.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="430" x="500" y="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;§2 — Monopoly Power + Exclusionary Conduct&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;United States v. Grinnell Corp.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;(1) Monopoly power in a relevant market.&lt;br&gt;(2) Willful acquisition or maintenance through exclusionary conduct.&lt;br&gt;(3) Interstate-commerce connection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;A superior product, business skill or historic accident can create lawful monopoly power.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="430" x="2300" y="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-0" edge="1" parent="1" source="start" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="s1" value="§1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-1" edge="1" parent="1" source="start" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="s2" value="§2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="entity" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Independent Centers of Decision Making?&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Copperweld • American Needle&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Parent + wholly owned subsidiary: one economic enterprise for §1.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Separately owned NFL teams remained independent actors when licensing logos; a common umbrella did not eliminate concerted action.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Economic reality controls.&lt;/b&gt; Partial ownership requires a fact-specific inquiry.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="430" x="500" y="670" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="single" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Single Enterprise → No §1 Agreement&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Copperweld&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Stop the §1 agreement inquiry if the challenged conduct is truly unilateral.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Still consider §2 if monopoly power and exclusionary conduct are present.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="430" x="-140" y="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="entity" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-3" edge="1" parent="1" source="entity" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="single" value="No independent actors">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="agree" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Was an Agreement Reached?&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Andreas • Foley • In re Text Messaging&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Direct proof: testimony, recordings, documents or communications showing assent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Circumstantial proof: parallel conduct &lt;b&gt;plus facts supporting agreement&lt;/b&gt;, such as invitations, assurances and enforcement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Foley: dinner discussion + assent + coordinated increases + pressure to comply supported conspiracy.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="430" x="500" y="1010" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="parallel" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Parallel Behavior Alone Is Insufficient&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;In re Text Messaging I / II&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Conscious parallelism does not itself establish a §1 agreement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Plausible allegations can permit discovery (I); after discovery, evidence must support a reasonable inference of actual agreement (II).&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="430" x="-170" y="1110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="entity" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="agree" value="Independent actors">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-5" edge="1" parent="1" source="agree" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="parallel" value="Insufficient evidence">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="standard" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Characterize the Restraint&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;BMI • NCAA • Sylvania • Leegin&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Is this a naked horizontal restraint, or part of a productive integration with plausible competitive benefits?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Do not choose per se merely because the arrangement affects price.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Choose the standard before applying it.&lt;/b&gt; Branches below are alternative analyses.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="430" x="500" y="1360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-6" edge="1" parent="1" source="agree" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="standard" value="Agreement established">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="perse" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Per Se Illegality&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Socony • Palmer • Catalano • Maricopa&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Naked horizontal price fixing, market allocation or equivalent restraints.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Price includes credit terms; price stabilization and maximum fees can also qualify.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;No proof of market power or actual price effects required; reasonable-price and ruinous-competition defenses fail.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" y="1720" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="quick" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Quick Look — Inherently Suspect Restraint&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;PolyGram Holding v. FTC&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Experience makes likely competitive harm apparent without a full market study.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Ask whether defendant offers a plausible, legally cognizable competitive justification.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;PolyGram: blocking discounts and ads for older recordings was not necessary to make the new joint album.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="500" y="1720" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ror" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rule of Reason — Full Competitive Inquiry&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;NCAA v. Alston • Realcomp&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Use when context and plausible efficiencies require fuller analysis.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Vertical nonprice restraints: &lt;i&gt;Sylvania&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Vertical minimum RPM: &lt;i&gt;Leegin&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Integrated blanket licensing: &lt;i&gt;BMI&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;These cases select an analytical standard; they do not automatically establish legality.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="1000" y="1720" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-7" edge="1" parent="1" source="standard" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="perse" value="Naked horizontal restraint">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-8" edge="1" parent="1" source="standard" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="quick" value="Obvious likely harm">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-9" edge="1" parent="1" source="standard" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="ror" value="Context / efficiencies matter">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="perend" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Per Se Result&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Trenton Potteries • Socony&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If agreement, qualifying restraint and commerce nexus are established → §1 violation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;An agreed “fair” price or a claimed public benefit does not excuse naked price fixing.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="430" y="2110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-10" edge="1" parent="1" source="perse" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="perend" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qend" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Test the Offered Justification&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;PolyGram • Professional Engineers&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;No plausible cognizable justification → condemn the inherently suspect restraint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If a plausible explanation is offered, address it: explain why harm remains clear or produce sufficient evidence of likely harm.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If competitive effects remain uncertain, use a fuller inquiry. A claim that competition itself is bad is not a competitive benefit.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="500" y="2110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-11" edge="1" parent="1" source="quick" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="qend" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="harm1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;1. Plaintiff Shows Substantial Harm&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Alston • Realcomp • NCAA&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Show harm to competition: higher prices, reduced output, worse quality or reduced choice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Use direct effects evidence or market definition, market power and evidence linking the restraint to likely harm.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Realcomp: restricting discount listings’ public exposure impaired competition in brokerage services.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="1000" y="2110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-12" edge="1" parent="1" source="ror" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="harm1" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="benefit1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;2. Defendant Shows Competitive Benefits&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Sylvania • Leegin • BMI&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Tie the claimed efficiency to the challenged restraint: dealer service, preventing free riding, lower transaction costs or creating a useful product.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Unsupported assertions or a desire to suppress competition do not suffice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If plaintiff fails to prove substantial harm, stop: no §1 violation established under this analysis.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="1000" y="2500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-13" edge="1" parent="1" source="harm1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="benefit1" value="Harm established">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="alt1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;3. Less Restrictive Alternatives&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Alston • Realcomp&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Plaintiff asks whether the claimed benefits could reasonably be achieved through substantially less restrictive means.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Alston: allowing education-related benefits could preserve the college-sports product without the challenged caps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Apply the governing burden framework to the evidence; avoid inventing ideal alternatives that would not work in practice.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="1000" y="2890" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-14" edge="1" parent="1" source="benefit1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="alt1" value="Cognizable benefits shown">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="result1" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;§1 Conclusion&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Alston • Professional Engineers&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If justification fails, or a workable less restrictive alternative establishes unreasonableness → violation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Otherwise assess remaining disputed net competitive effects under the applicable rule-of-reason framework; plaintiff retains the ultimate burden.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;State the restraint, analytical standard, decisive facts and conclusion.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="430" x="1000" y="3280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-15" edge="1" parent="1" source="alt1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="result1" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="market" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;1. Define the Relevant Market&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Du Pont • Kodak • Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Product:&lt;/b&gt; reasonable interchangeability and substitution in use, quality and price.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Geography:&lt;/b&gt; where customers can realistically turn.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Beware the cellophane fallacy: substitution at an already monopolized price can overstate alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Kodak: lock-in and information costs can support separate brand-specific aftermarkets.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="430" x="2300" y="670" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-16" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="market" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="power" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;2. Establish Monopoly Power&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Alcoa • Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Ability to control prices or exclude competition; evaluate durable share together with barriers and competitive conditions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Microsoft: very high OS share + applications barrier to entry; user/developer feedback protected the installed base.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Alcoa’s 90% / 64% / 33% discussion illustrates market-definition effects, not fixed universal legal cutoffs.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="430" x="2300" y="1060" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-17" edge="1" parent="1" source="market" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="power" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nopower" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;No Monopoly Power?&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Grinnell • Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Completed monopolization is not established without monopoly power.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If facts support it, separately consider attempted monopolization: exclusionary conduct, specific intent and dangerous probability of success in a relevant market.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Microsoft’s browser-attempt claim failed for inadequate market proof.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="430" x="1800" y="1060" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-18" edge="1" parent="1" source="power" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="nopower" value="Not established">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="conduct" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;3. Identify Exclusionary Conduct&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Microsoft • Aspen Skiing&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Identify the precise acts and their competitive effects; injury to a rival alone is insufficient.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Does the conduct impair the competitive process, rather than reflect merits competition?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Use the appropriate conduct-specific analysis (right), then return to the burden framework below.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="430" x="2300" y="1450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-19" edge="1" parent="1" source="power" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="conduct" value="Power established">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="refusal" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Refusal to Deal — Narrow Exception&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Aspen Skiing • Trinko • Otter Tail&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;No general duty to help rivals. Aspen: termination of voluntary profitable dealing, rejected retail sales and sacrificed short-run profits supported exclusion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Trinko: compelled sharing and active regulation distinguished Aspen; regulatory violations do not themselves establish §2 liability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Otter Tail: withholding wholesale supply and essential transmission blocked municipal competition.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="430" x="2800" y="1450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="exclusive" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Exclusive Dealing — Foreclosure&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Google Search (2024) • Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Identify practical exclusivity, even if not expressly complete.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Evaluate substantial foreclosure: amount and quality of access blocked, contract duration, termination rights and alternative channels.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Google: default-search deals blocked distribution and rivals’ query scale. Assess exclusion, not merely Google’s popularity.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="2800" y="1880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tying" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tying — Distinguish §1 and §2&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Jefferson Parish • Kodak • Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;§1 traditional tying: separate demand, conditioned sale, appreciable tying-market power and substantial tied commerce.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Jefferson Parish lacked sufficient power; Kodak survived summary judgment because aftermarket power was factually disputed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Microsoft’s platform-software tying required rule of reason under §1. Integration may separately be exclusionary under §2; assess effects and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="430" x="2800" y="2270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-20" edge="1" parent="1" source="conduct" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="refusal" value="Refusal to deal">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-21" edge="1" parent="1" source="refusal" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="exclusive" value="Other conduct to check">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-22" edge="1" parent="1" source="exclusive" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="tying" value="Other conduct to check">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="harm2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;4. Plaintiff Shows Anticompetitive Effects&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;United States v. Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Connect the act to harm to the competitive process and consumers: exclusion, higher costs, reduced choice or impaired innovation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Intent can illuminate likely effects, but intent or a rival’s loss alone does not establish exclusion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;OEM restrictions and code commingling hindered emerging browser/platform threats.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="2300" y="1840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-23" edge="1" parent="1" source="conduct" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="harm2" value="Apply to each challenged act">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="benefit2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;5. Defendant Gives a Procompetitive Justification&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Microsoft • Aspen Skiing&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Identify a supported efficiency or consumer benefit linked to the act: performance, security, quality or other merits-based reason.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Copyright or product-design labels do not automatically defeat scrutiny.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If plaintiff fails to establish anticompetitive effects, that challenged act does not establish exclusionary conduct.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="430" x="2300" y="2230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-24" edge="1" parent="1" source="harm2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="benefit2" value="Harm established">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="weigh2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;6. Rebut or Weigh the Justification&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;United States v. Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Plaintiff may rebut the justification. If it remains unrebutted, plaintiff must show competitive harm outweighs the benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;No supported justification after proven harm → exclusionary conduct.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Keep conduct-specific limits in view; ordinary hard competition is not unlawful simply because rivals lose.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="430" x="2300" y="2620" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-25" edge="1" parent="1" source="benefit2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="weigh2" value="Justification offered">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cause" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;7. Connect Exclusion to Monopoly Maintenance&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;United States v. Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Ask whether conduct is reasonably capable of contributing significantly to continued monopoly power.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;For nascent threats, liability does not require certainty about how competition would have developed without exclusion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Distinguish evidence sufficient for liability from the causal showing needed to justify a particular remedy.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="430" x="2300" y="3010" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-26" edge="1" parent="1" source="weigh2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="cause" value="Exclusion established">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="result2" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;§2 Conclusion&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Grinnell • Microsoft&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Monopoly power + exclusionary acquisition/maintenance + adequate causal connection → monopolization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Lawfully acquired power, high prices or success alone do not establish the offense.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;If completed monopolization fails, analyze any supported attempt claim separately; do not assume an agreement is necessary for single-firm §2 liability.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="430" x="2300" y="3400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="flow-edge-27" edge="1" parent="1" source="cause" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;endArrow=classic;fontSize=13;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="result2" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;spacing=2;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:6px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;How to Use This Flowchart&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:5px 4px&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Class slides + existing chart notes + Important Cases tab&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;Follow the main §1 or §2 spine downward; read the side branches when those facts appear. Check both statutes where an agreement also preserves monopoly power.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;§1 rule-of-reason steps follow Alston/Realcomp; §2 steps follow Microsoft. Do not mechanically substitute one framework for the other.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:7px 10px&quot;&gt;This tab focuses on the course’s §§1–2 material. Clayton Act §7 merger analysis belongs in a separate inquiry.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="930" x="1800" y="3790" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
